From: Alan Shearer
Subject: Network prefs: keep saved gateway when live default route is gone

InterfaceAddressView fills Gateway from GetDefaultGateway() on the live
routing table. ifconfig down deletes that route; the interfaces file
still has the static gateway. The field goes blank, and Apply writes
the empty value back (GetMessage omits an unset gateway).

If the live lookup fails, show the saved BNetworkInterfaceAddressSettings
gateway. On Apply in Static mode, keep the previous saved gateway when
the field is empty instead of dropping it.

Does not restore the live default route. That is net_server.

Coldfirex/haiku-fixes#1
https://dev.haiku-os.org/ticket/9695
https://dev.haiku-os.org/ticket/16349

diff --git a/src/preferences/network/InterfaceAddressView.cpp b/src/preferences/network/InterfaceAddressView.cpp
--- a/src/preferences/network/InterfaceAddressView.cpp
+++ b/src/preferences/network/InterfaceAddressView.cpp
@@ -241,8 +241,18 @@
 	BNetworkAddress gateway;
 	if (fInterface.GetDefaultGateway(fFamily, gateway) == B_OK)
 		fGatewayField->SetText(gateway.ToString());
-	else
-		fGatewayField->SetText(NULL);
+	else {
+		// Live table has no default route. ifconfig down drops it;
+		// the saved profile may still have a static gateway.
+		BNetworkInterfaceSettings saved(interfaceSettings);
+		int32 savedIndex = saved.FindFirstAddress(fFamily);
+		if (savedIndex >= 0
+			&& !saved.AddressAt(savedIndex).Gateway().IsEmpty()) {
+			fGatewayField->SetText(
+				saved.AddressAt(savedIndex).Gateway().ToString());
+		} else
+			fGatewayField->SetText(NULL);
+	}
 }
 
 
@@ -322,6 +332,8 @@
 	settings.SetFamily(fFamily);
 	settings.SetAutoConfigure(mode == kModeAuto);
 
+	BNetworkAddress previousGateway = settings.Gateway();
+
 	settings.Address().Unset();
 	settings.Mask().Unset();
 	settings.Peer().Unset();
@@ -332,6 +344,8 @@
 		_SetAddress(settings.Address(), fAddressField->Text());
 		_SetAddress(settings.Mask(), fNetmaskField->Text());
 		_SetAddress(settings.Gateway(), fGatewayField->Text());
+		if (settings.Gateway().IsEmpty() && !previousGateway.IsEmpty())
+			settings.Gateway() = previousGateway;
 	}
 }
 
